.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBlibXm\fP contains its own copy of the XPM library (the code of
libXpm 3\&.5\&.12, which implements version 3\&.4k of the XPM interface),
which it uses to read the XPM pixmaps and icons named in resources and
by \fBXmGetPixmap\fP(3)\&. Its functions are exported with an
\fBXme\fP prefix so that they do not clash with a system \fBlibXpm\fP
loaded into the same process\&. \fB<Xm/XpmP\&.h>\fP declares them and
defines the usual XPM names as macros for them (\fBXpmReadFileToPixmap\fP
for \fBXmeXpmReadFileToPixmap\fP, and so on), together with the XPM
types (\fBXpmAttributes\fP, \fBXpmImage\fP, \fBXpmInfo\fP,
\fBXpmColor\fP, \fBXpmColorSymbol\fP, \fBXpmExtension\fP), the
attribute mask bits (\fBXpmVisual\fP, \fBXpmColormap\fP,
\fBXpmSize\fP, \&.\&.\&.) and the status codes\&.
.PP
Each function behaves as the XPM function of the same name without the
\fBXme\fP prefix, which the XPM Manual (Arnaud Le Hors, \fIXPM Manual,
The X PixMap Format\fP) and the \fBlibXpm\fP manual pages describe in
detail\&. In summary:
.IP "\fBXmeXpmReadFileTo\fP\fItype\fP" 10
reads an XPM file into a pixmap and its shape mask, an \fBXImage\fP
and its shape image, an \fBXpmImage\fP and \fBXpmInfo\fP, a buffer
holding the file contents, or an array of strings ("data", as an XPM
file included in C source)\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmWriteFileFrom\fP\fItype\fP" 10
writes one of those representations to an XPM file\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmCreate\fP\fIto\fP\fBFrom\fP\fIfrom\fP" 10
converts between the representations without a file\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmFree\fP\fIthing\fP" 10
frees the memory that the other functions allocated\&. Free returned
buffers and data arrays with \fBXmeXpmFree\fP, and the contents of an
\fBXpmAttributes\fP, \fBXpmImage\fP or \fBXpmInfo\fP filled in by
them with \fBXmeXpmFreeAttributes\fP, \fBXmeXpmFreeXpmImage\fP and
\fBXmeXpmFreeXpmInfo\fP\&. Free pixmaps and images with
\fBXFreePixmap\fP(3) and \fBXDestroyImage\fP(3)\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmAttributesSize\fP" 10
returns \fBsizeof(XpmAttributes)\fP as compiled into the library\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmGetErrorString\fP" 10
returns a static string describing a status code\&.
.IP "\fBXmeXpmLibraryVersion\fP" 10
returns the version of the XPM code, \fBXpmIncludeVersion\fP, which
is 30411 (3\&.4k)\&.
.PP
This copy differs from \fBlibXpm\fP in two ways\&. It never runs
external programs: a file whose name ends in \fB\&.Z\fP or \fB\&.gz\fP
is read as an uncompressed XPM file (and is therefore normally rejected
as invalid), and the writers always write uncompressed files whatever
the file name\&. It also does not provide \fBXpmGetParseError\fP,
although \fB<Xm/XpmP\&.h>\fP declares it\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
The functions returning \fBint\fP, other than
\fBXmeXpmAttributesSize\fP and \fBXmeXpmLibraryVersion\fP, return one
of:
.IP "\fBXpmSuccess\fP" 10
The function succeeded\&.
.IP "\fBXpmColorError\fP" 10
The image was created, but some colors could not be allocated exactly
and the closest ones were used\&.
.IP "\fBXpmOpenFailed\fP" 10
The file could not be opened\&.
.IP "\fBXpmFileInvalid\fP" 10
The file or data is not valid XPM\&.
.IP "\fBXpmNoMemory\fP" 10
Memory was exhausted\&.
.IP "\fBXpmColorFailed\fP" 10
A color could not be allocated and no fallback was possible\&.
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
\fB<Xm/XpmP\&.h>\fP and \fB<X11/xpm\&.h>\fP define the same names and
must not both be included\&. Programs that do not depend on the copy in
\fBlibXm\fP should use the system \fBlibXpm\fP instead\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmGetPixmap\fP(3), \fBXmGetPixmapByDepth\fP(3) and
\fBXmInstallImage\fP(3)\&.
